## PLATFORM CONTEXT — AGENT DEPLOYMENT

### Core rules (all platforms)
- Agent types: Windows Agent, Mac Agent, Linux Agent (V2 only — V1 is EOL, remove on sight)
- Each agent gets a unique UUID. **Never image/clone after agent install** — install agent post-clone
- Agent → N-sight cloud over HTTPS TLS 1.2+. TLS 1.0/1.1 are blocked
- Only current + previous GA releases supported. Use GA in production, never RC
- Always assign a **Monitoring Template** at install time — never rely on Standard checks default

### Windows
- Preferred deploy: All Devices → Add Devices → download RW package → deploy via Intune/GPO/script
- Package bakes in Client+Site auth — no manual login at endpoint
- Manual install: run as Administrator, set proxy **before** entering credentials (use IP, not NetBIOS)
- Workstation vs Server mode: only selectable on workstations; servers always install as Server
- Name devices meaningfully — name appears in dashboard, alerts, reports (e.g. `hostname-dept-loc`)
- If package credentials change → regenerate the package

### macOS
- Preferred deploy: RW package via MDM (Jamf / ABM / N-sight DMA) for zero-touch
- Only Remote Worker installer available for Mac — no legacy site package
- Post-install: grant **Full Disk Access + Accessibility** in System Settings → Privacy & Security
- Take Control also needs **Screen Recording** permission
- Pre-approve PKG via MDM profile to avoid Gatekeeper blocks
- Use Device Management for Apple (DMA) for corporate fleet where possible

### Linux
- **V2 agent only** — check for and replace any V1 installations
- All Linux = Server mode (no workstation mode)
- Preferred deploy: RW package → `chmod +x *.sh && sudo ./AGENT_CLIENT_SITE_RW.sh`
- Manual: `sudo dpkg -i agent.deb` (Debian/Ubuntu) or `sudo rpm -i agent.rpm` (RHEL/Fedora)
- Verify TLS 1.2: `openssl s_client -connect <territory-url>:443 -tls1_2`
- Firewall: outbound TCP 443 to territory URL required — no inbound ports needed
- Supported distros vary by feature — check https://documentation.n-able.com/remote-management/userguide/Content/linux_os.htm before deploying checks

